{title: 498 - Still, Still With Thee}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D/A]Still, [Em/G]still [D/F#]with Thee, [G/D]when [D]purple morning [G#dim]breaketh,
[A]When [Em/B]the [D/A]bird [Em/B]waketh, [G]and [A/E]the [D/A]shadows flee;
[D/A]Fairer than morning, [Bm]lovelier than daylight,
[A]Dawns [Em/B]the [D/A]sweet [Em/B]consciousness, [A7/G]I [G]am with [D/F#]Thee.

Verse 2:
[D/A]Alone with Thee, [G/D]amid [D]the mystic [G#dim]shadows,
[A]The [Em/B]solemn hush of [G]nature [D/A]newly born;
[D/A]Alone with Thee [F#m]in [Bm]breathless [Em/B]adoration,
[A]In [Em/B]the [D/A]calm [Em/B]dew and [G]freshness of the [D/F#]morn.

Verse 3:
[D/A]Still, [Em/G]still [D/F#]with Thee! [G/D]As [D]to each newborn [G#dim]morning
[A]A fresh [Em/B]and [D/A]solemn [Em/G]splendor [A/E]still [D/A]is [A7/G]given,
[D/A]So [Em/G]does [D/F#]this blessed [F#m]consciousness, [Em/B]awaking,
[A]Breathe each [Em/B]day [D/A]nearness [Em/G]unto [A7/G]Thee [G]and heaven.

Verse 4:
[D/A]So [Em/G]shall [D/F#]it be [G/D]at [D]last, in that [A/E]bright [G#dim]morning,
[A]When the [Em/B]soul [D/A]waketh [Em/G]and [G]life's [D/A]shadows flee;
[D/A]O [Em/G]in [D/F#]that hour, [F#m]fairer [Bm]than [Em/B]daylight [Bm]dawning,
[A]Shall [Em/B]rise [D/A]the [Em/B]glorious [G]thought, [A7/G]I [G]am with [D/F#]Thee.
